          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
            equipped with an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            on an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            (often: a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+action"} group action
            on
            = succeed ")," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %strong invariant
            of the action is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+element"} element
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            which is taken by the action to itself, hence which is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fixed+point"} fixed point
            for all the operations of the monoid.
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %p
            A robust definition of invariants that generalizes to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            is via the expression of actions as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+groupoids"} action groupoids
            regarded as sitting over
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoids"} groupoids
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-action"} infinity-action
            and at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+representations+and+associated+bundles"} geometry of physics – representations and associated bundles
          %p
            We describe how the ordinary concept of invariants is recovered from this perspective and then consider its immediate generalizations to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-topos+theory"} (infinity,1)-topos theory
            and its formalization in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
          %h3#ViaSectionsOfActionGroupoidProjections Via sections of action groupoid projections
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+group"} discrete group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
              a
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
              on some set
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariants"} invariants
              of that action is equivalent to the groupoid of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sections"} sections
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+groupoid"} action groupoid
              projection of
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "geometry+of+physics+--+representations+and+associated+bundles#MapFromActionGroupoidOnSetBackToBG"} this proposition
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "geometry+of+physics+--+representations+and+associated+bundles#EquivalenceOfPermutationRepresentationsWithActionGroupodsInSlice"} this proposition
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              The sections in question are diagrams in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grpd"} Grpd
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mi G
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi σ
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi S
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi G
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi id
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ⇙
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↙
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi p
                                    %mi ρ
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mi G
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\mathbf{B}G &amp;&amp; \stackrel{\sigma}{\longrightarrow} &amp;&amp; S//G
                    \\\
                    \&amp; {}_{\mathllap{id}}\searrow
                    \&amp;\swArrow_{\mathrlap{\simeq}}&amp;
                    \\swarrow_{\mathrlap{p_\rho}}
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; \mathbf{B}G
                    }
                    \\,,
            %p
              hence the groupoid which they form is equivalently the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-groupoid"} hom-groupoid
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Grpd
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi id
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi G
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mi ρ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Grpd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Grpd_{/\mathbf{B}G}(id_{\mathbf{B}G}, p_\rho)
                    \\in Grpd
            %p
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} slice
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grpd"} Grpd
              over
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "geometry+of+physics+--+representations+and+associated+bundles#IntertwinersOfPermutationActionAsSliceHoms"} this proposition
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mi ρ
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (p_\rho)_\bullet
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "geometry+of+physics+--+representations+and+associated+bundles#MapFromActionGroupoidOnSetBackToBG"} this proposition
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mi G
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo •
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi σ
                                  %mo •
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi S
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi G
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo •
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi id
                                    %mo •
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↙
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %msub
                                    %mi p
                                    %mi ρ
                                  %msub
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                    %mo •
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mi G
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo •
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    (\mathbf{B}G)_\bullet &amp;&amp; \stackrel{\sigma_\bullet}{\longrightarrow} &amp;&amp; (S//G)_\bullet
                    \\\
                    \&amp; {}_{\mathllap{id_\bullet}}\searrow &amp;=&amp; \swarrow_{\mathrlap{(p_\rho)_\bullet}}
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; (\mathbf{B}G)_\bullet
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              These
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
              now are manifestly functors that are the identity on the group labels of the morphisms
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi σ
                      %mo •
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo *
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mi g
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo *
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ↦
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi σ
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mo *
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mi g
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi σ
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mo *
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %mo =
                              %mi ρ
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi σ
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mo *
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi g
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\sigma_\bullet
                    \\;\colon\;
                    \\left(
                    \\array{
                    \\ast
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{g}}
                    \\\
                    \\ast
                    }
                    \\right)
                    \\;\;
                    \\mapsto
                    \\;\;
                    \\left(
                    \\array{
                    \\sigma(\ast)
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{g}}
                    \\\
                    \\sigma(\ast) &amp; = \rho(\sigma(\ast)(g))
                    }
                    \\right)
                    \\,.
            %p
              This shows that they pick precisely those elements
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma(\ast) \in S
              which are fixed by the
              = succeed "-action" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ρ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
            %p
              Moreover, since these functors are identity on the group labels, there are no non-trivial
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphisms"} natural isomorphisms
              between them, and hence the groupoid of sections is indeed a set, the set of invariant elements.
          %p More generally, we may consider sections of these groupoid projections after pulling them back along some cocycle:
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              Given an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associated+bundle"} associated bundle
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mi G
                    %mi V
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \times_G V\to X
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modulating+morphism"} modulated
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "geometry+of+physics+--+representations+and+associated+bundles#Associated1BundleAsPullbackOfActionGroupoid"} this proposition
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+groupoids"} smooth groupoids
              of the form
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi X
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \colon X \longrightarrow \mathbf{B}G
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sections"} sections
              is equivalently the groupoid of diagrams
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi σ
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi S
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi G
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi g
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ⇙
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↙
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi p
                                    %mi ρ
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mi G
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X &amp;&amp; \stackrel{\sigma}{\longrightarrow} &amp;&amp; S//G
                    \\\
                    \&amp; {}_{\mathllap{g}}\searrow
                    \&amp;\swArrow_{\mathrlap{\simeq}}&amp; \swarrow_{\mathrlap{p_\rho}}
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; \mathbf{B}G
                    }
                    \\,,
            %p
              hence the groupoid of sections is the slice
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-groupoid"} hom-groupoid
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi P
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mi G
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi Grpd
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mi ρ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Gamma_X(P\times_G V)
                    \\simeq
                    Grpd_{/\mathbf{B}G}(g, p_\rho)
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              By the defining
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "geometry+of+physics+--+representations+and+associated+bundles#Associated1BundleAsPullbackOfActionGroupoid"} this proposition
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              Taken together this means that
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariants"} invariants
              of group actions are equivalently the sections of the corresponding
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+principal+bundle"} universal
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associated+bundle"} associated bundle
          %h3#ForInfinityGroupActions
            Invariants of
            = succeed "-group" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Grp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G \in Grp(\mathbf{H})
            an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-group"} ∞-group
            and
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo *
                  %mo :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo ⊢
                  %mo :
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi Type
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  * : \mathbf{B} G \vdash : V(*) : Type
          %p
            an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-action"} ∞-action
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo ∈
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \in \mathbf{H}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+product"} dependent product
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⊢
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mo *
                      %mo :
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi G
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi Type
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\vdash \prod_{* : \mathbf{B}G} V(*) : Type
                  \\,.
          %p
            The connected components of this is equivalently the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+cohomology"} group cohomology
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-module"} infinity-module
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
          %h2#properties Properties
          #TakingInvariantsForFiniteGroupCommutesWithTaingHomologyInCharZero.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (in
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+zero"} characteristic zero
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariants"} invariants
                for
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+group"} finite group
                are compatible with
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+homology"} chain homology
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mo •
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (V_\bullet, \partial)
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
              over a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+field"} ground field
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+zero"} characteristic zero
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
              by a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+group"} finite group
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              = succeed "-invariants" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+homology"} chain homology
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mo •
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ∂
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mo •
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi G
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H_\bullet((V_\bullet,\partial)^G)
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    H_\bullet((V_\bullet,\partial))^G
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              Since the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+field"} ground field
              has
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+zero"} characteristic zero
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+averaging"} group averaging
              exists and provides a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+map"} linear map
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi V
                              %mo •
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi p
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mi V
                              %mo •
                              %mi G
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi x
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↦
                          %mtd
                            %mfrac
                              %mn 1
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                %mi G
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %munder
                              %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                              %mrow
                                %mi g
                                %mo ∈
                                %mi G
                            %mi g
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    V_\bullet &amp; \overset{p}{\longrightarrow} &amp; V_\bullet^G
                    \\\
                    x &amp;\mapsto&amp; \frac{1}{{\vert G \vert}} \underset{g \in G}{\sum} g(x)
                    }
            %p
              onto the
              = succeed "-invariants." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %p
              Now for a
              = succeed "-class" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+homology"} chain homology
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mo •
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [x] \in H_\bullet((V_\bullet,\partial))
              being
              = succeed "-invariant" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ≔
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g[x] \coloneqq [g(x)] = [x]
              for all
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \in G
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [x] = [p(x)]
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cycles"} cycles
              to invariant
              = succeed "-classes" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+homology"} chain homology
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi V
                      %mo •
                      %mi G
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mo •
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Z((V_\bullet^G,\partial)) \longrightarrow H_\bullet((V_\bullet,\partial))
            %p
              is an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphism"} epimorphism
            %p
              Next consider the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel"} kernel
              of this map, which a priori is
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msubsup
                        %mi V
                        %mo •
                        %mi G
                      %mo ,
                      %mo ∂
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∩
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mo •
                      %mo ,
                      %mo ∂
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z((V_\bullet^G,\partial)) \cap B((V_\bullet,\partial))
              = succeed "-invariant" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundaries"} boundaries
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi V
                      %mo •
                      %mi G
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mo •
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi V
                      %mo •
                      %mi G
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Z((V_\bullet^G,\partial)) \cap B((V_\bullet,\partial))
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    B((V_\bullet^G, \partial))
                    \\,.
            %p
              It is clear that there is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+map"} inclusion
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi V
                      %mo •
                      %mi G
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi V
                      %mo •
                      %mi G
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mo •
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    B((V_\bullet^G, \partial))
                    \\hookrightarrow
                    Z((V_\bullet^G,\partial)) \cap B((V_\bullet,\partial))
            %p
              so it only remains to see that this is also a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surjection"} surjection
            %p To that end, consider any
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi V
                      %mo •
                      %mi G
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mo •
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    x \in Z((V_\bullet^G,\partial)) \cap B((V_\bullet,\partial))
                    \\,.
            %p
              Since in particular
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mo •
                      %mo ,
                      %mo ∂
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in B((V_\bullet,\partial))
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \in V_\bullet
              with
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo =
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x = \partial y
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in V_\bullet(G)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo =
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    x = p(x) = p(\partial y) = \partial(p y)
            %p and hence that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi V
                      %mo •
                      %mi G
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    x \in B((V_\bullet^G,\partial))
                    \\,.
